# Configurable checkout targets for the repos this integration test spans.
# Sourced by scripts/checkout-repos.sh. Override any of these by exporting the
# same variable before running the script -- in CI, each *_REF is wired to a
# workflow_dispatch input (core_repo_ref / signer_repo_ref / seeder_repo_ref) via
# a job-level `env:` entry in .github/workflows/weekly-integration-test.yml, which
# this file's `${VAR:-default}` fallback picks up automatically since the var is
# already exported by the time this file is sourced.

# --- tapyrus-signer -----------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: SIGNER_REPO_REF defaults to 163_federationChangeTomlSetup -- a diverged
# sibling branch on this fork (NOT a descendant of master), chosen because it has
# a real tapyrus-setup CLI for the federation-setup + genesis-signing ceremony
# (verified end-to-end, see doc/legacy-readme.md and doc/weekly-integration-test-plan.md).
# That upstream branch itself does NOT build out of the box (see doc/legacy-readme.md
# "Dockerfile notes" -- toolchain pin + gmp-mpfr-sys c-no-tests feature needed). Those
# fixes are committed, but only on a local branch, `federation-setup-review`, based on
# top of 163_federationChangeTomlSetup -- not pushed anywhere. For local testing with
# those fixes applied, override BOTH:
#   SIGNER_REPO_URL=/path/to/local/tapyrus-signer SIGNER_REPO_REF=federation-setup-review
SIGNER_REPO_URL="${SIGNER_REPO_URL:-https://github.com/Naviabheeman/tapyrus-signer.git}"
SIGNER_REPO_REF="${SIGNER_REPO_REF:-163_federationChangeTomlSetup}"

# --- tapyrus-core ---------------------------------------------------------
CORE_REPO_URL="${CORE_REPO_URL:-https://github.com/chaintope/tapyrus-core.git}"
CORE_REPO_REF="${CORE_REPO_REF:-master}"

# --- tapyrus-seeder ---------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: SEEDER_REPO_REF defaults to master, but master does NOT have the four bug
# fixes (build failure, sprintf buffer overflow, two data races) documented in
# doc/work-done.md -- those only exist on a local, unpushed `docker-build-fix`
# branch today. Override SEEDER_REPO_REF once that branch (or an equivalent fix)
# is pushed somewhere reachable, e.g.:
#   SEEDER_REPO_URL=/path/to/local/tapyrus-seeder SEEDER_REPO_REF=docker-build-fix
SEEDER_REPO_URL="${SEEDER_REPO_URL:-https://github.com/chaintope/tapyrus-seeder.git}"
SEEDER_REPO_REF="${SEEDER_REPO_REF:-master}"
